[
  {
    "text": "The cartoon ran in every",
    "start": 0.03,
    "end": 1.53
  },
  {
    "text": "Hearst paper in America.",
    "start": 1.53,
    "end": 3.12
  },
  {
    "text": "A fat man in a",
    "start": 3.15,
    "end": 3.84
  },
  {
    "text": "suit covered in dollar signs,",
    "start": 3.84,
    "end": 5.68
  },
  {
    "text": "smoking a cigar the size",
    "start": 5.71,
    "end": 7.12
  },
  {
    "text": "of his forearm.",
    "start": 7.12,
    "end": 8.14
  },
  {
    "text": "The caption changed every week.",
    "start": 8.27,
    "end": 10.08
  },
  {
    "text": "The man did not.",
    "start": 10.19,
    "end": 11.36
  },
  {
    "text": "His name was Mark Hanna,",
    "start": 11.39,
    "end": 12.92
  },
  {
    "text": "and in 1896, he did",
    "start": 13.07,
    "end": 14.6
  },
  {
    "text": "something no one had ever",
    "start": 14.6,
    "end": 15.78
  },
  {
    "text": "done at that scale.",
    "start": 15.78,
    "end": 16.78
  },
  {
    "text": "He turned the American presidential",
    "start": 16.85,
    "end": 18.38
  },
  {
    "text": "election into a corporate purchase",
    "start": 18.53,
    "end": 20.34
  },
  {
    "text": "order, three and a half",
    "start": 20.34,
    "end": 21.54
  },
  {
    "text": "million dollars raised, 20 times",
    "start": 21.55,
    "end": 23.64
  },
  {
    "text": "what his opponent spent.",
    "start": 23.64,
    "end": 25.1
  },
  {
    "text": "Banks assessed at a quarter",
    "start": 25.13,
    "end": 26.94
  },
  {
    "text": "of a percent of capital,",
    "start": 26.94,
    "end": 28.68
  },
  {
    "text": "railroads shaken down personally.",
    "start": 28.71,
    "end": 31.08
  },
  {
    "text": "Standard oil, $250,000.",
    "start": 31.11,
    "end": 34.12
  },
  {
    "text": "J.P.",
    "start": 34.15,
    "end": 34.7
  },
  {
    "text": "Morgan, $250,000.",
    "start": 34.7,
    "end": 37.12
  },
  {
    "text": "Half a million voters transported",
    "start": 37.15,
    "end": 38.68
  },
  {
    "text": "by train to shake one",
    "start": 38.83,
    "end": 40.11
  },
  {
    "text": "man's hand.",
    "start": 40.11,
    "end": 40.96
  },
  {
    "text": "200 million pieces of campaign",
    "start": 41.03,
    "end": 42.77
  },
  {
    "text": "literature printed and mailed.",
    "start": 42.77,
    "end": 44.68
  },
  {
    "text": "The opposition had a 36-year-old",
    "start": 44.71,
    "end": 46.69
  },
  {
    "text": "preacher who could move a",
    "start": 46.71,
    "end": 48.19
  },
  {
    "text": "crowd to tears.",
    "start": 48.19,
    "end": 49.28
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna had a ledger.",
    "start": 49.31,
    "end": 50.52
  },
  {
    "text": "And when November came, the",
    "start": 50.55,
    "end": 52.04
  },
  {
    "text": "ledger won.",
    "start": 52.04,
    "end": 52.68
  },
  {
    "text": "He wasn't born with money.",
    "start": 52.71,
    "end": 54.18
  },
  {
    "text": "He was born in a",
    "start": 54.21,
    "end": 55.04
  },
  {
    "text": "grocery.",
    "start": 55.04,
    "end": 55.74
  },
  {
    "text": "New Lisbon, Ohio, 1837.",
    "start": 55.83,
    "end": 58.47
  },
  {
    "text": "His father, Dr.",
    "start": 58.51,
    "end": 59.38
  },
  {
    "text": "Leonard Hanna, was a country",
    "start": 59.38,
    "end": 60.68
  },
  {
    "text": "physician who ran a wholesale",
    "start": 60.68,
    "end": 62.21
  },
  {
    "text": "grocery on the side.",
    "start": 62.21,
    "end": 63.56
  },
  {
    "text": "Flour, salt, dry goods to",
    "start": 63.59,
    "end": 65.31
  },
  {
    "text": "Ohio farmers.",
    "start": 65.31,
    "end": 66.25
  },
  {
    "text": "When Mark was 15, the",
    "start": 66.47,
    "end": 67.79
  },
  {
    "text": "family moved to Cleveland.",
    "start": 67.79,
    "end": 69.4
  },
  {
    "text": "He enrolled at Western Reserve",
    "start": 69.43,
    "end": 71.22
  },
  {
    "text": "College.",
    "start": 71.22,
    "end": 71.74
  },
  {
    "text": "In his class was a",
    "start": 71.77,
    "end": 72.86
  },
  {
    "text": "quiet, awkward boy who would",
    "start": 72.86,
    "end": 74.71
  },
  {
    "text": "grow up to control 90%",
    "start": 74.71,
    "end": 76.4
  },
  {
    "text": "of the oil-refining capacity in",
    "start": 76.43,
    "end": 78.35
  },
  {
    "text": "the United States.",
    "start": 78.35,
    "end": 79.72
  },
  {
    "text": "His name was John D.",
    "start": 79.75,
    "end": 80.92
  },
  {
    "text": "Rockefeller.",
    "start": 80.92,
    "end": 81.88
  },
  {
    "text": "The two would orbit each",
    "start": 81.91,
    "end": 82.83
  },
  {
    "text": "other for the next 40",
    "start": 82.83,
    "end": 84.24
  },
  {
    "text": "years.",
    "start": 84.24,
    "end": 84.84
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna lasted one year at",
    "start": 84.87,
    "end": 86.07
  },
  {
    "text": "Western Reserve before he quit,",
    "start": 86.07,
    "end": 87.82
  },
  {
    "text": "not because he was failing,",
    "start": 87.85,
    "end": 89.28
  },
  {
    "text": "because he had already figured",
    "start": 89.31,
    "end": 90.26
  },
  {
    "text": "out something the professors couldn't",
    "start": 90.35,
    "end": 92.04
  },
  {
    "text": "teach.",
    "start": 92.19,
    "end": 92.6
  },
  {
    "text": "The real education was in",
    "start": 92.63,
    "end": 93.95
  },
  {
    "text": "the price of things.",
    "start": 93.95,
    "end": 95.2
  },
  {
    "text": "He went back to the",
    "start": 95.23,
    "end": 96.03
  },
  {
    "text": "store, worked the floor, watched",
    "start": 96.03,
    "end": 97.96
  },
  {
    "text": "how men negotiated, watched who",
    "start": 97.96,
    "end": 99.93
  },
  {
    "text": "paid on time and who",
    "start": 99.93,
    "end": 100.84
  },
  {
    "text": "didn't, watched which suppliers had",
    "start": 100.99,
    "end": 103.01
  },
  {
    "text": "leverage and which ones begged.",
    "start": 103.01,
    "end": 104.68
  },
  {
    "text": "Then the Civil War came.",
    "start": 104.71,
    "end": 105.92
  },
  {
    "text": "He served briefly, came home,",
    "start": 105.95,
    "end": 108.14
  },
  {
    "text": "and married a woman named",
    "start": 108.17,
    "end": 109.35
  },
  {
    "text": "Charlotte Rhodes.",
    "start": 109.35,
    "end": 110.46
  },
  {
    "text": "Her father was Daniel Rhodes,",
    "start": 110.49,
    "end": 112.2
  },
  {
    "text": "Cole and Iron, one of",
    "start": 112.2,
    "end": 114.12
  },
  {
    "text": "the men quietly getting rich",
    "start": 114.17,
    "end": 115.68
  },
  {
    "text": "off everything Cleveland was becoming.",
    "start": 115.77,
    "end": 118.12
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna walked into that business",
    "start": 118.15,
    "end": 119.44
  },
  {
    "text": "and never walked out.",
    "start": 119.44,
    "end": 120.76
  },
  {
    "text": "By 1867, Marcus Alonso Hanna",
    "start": 120.79,
    "end": 123.16
  },
  {
    "text": "had built M.A.",
    "start": 123.19,
    "end": 124.14
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna and Company, a coal",
    "start": 124.23,
    "end": 125.73
  },
  {
    "text": "and iron brokerage sitting at",
    "start": 125.73,
    "end": 127.68
  },
  {
    "text": "the exact pivot point where",
    "start": 127.68,
    "end": 129.46
  },
  {
    "text": "Lake Erie ore boats unloaded",
    "start": 129.46,
    "end": 131.02
  },
  {
    "text": "for the Pittsburgh Steel Mills.",
    "start": 131.02,
    "end": 132.72
  },
  {
    "text": "Cleveland was the choke point",
    "start": 132.75,
    "end": 134.28
  },
  {
    "text": "and Hanna sat on it.",
    "start": 134.43,
    "end": 135.41
  },
  {
    "text": "Every ton of iron ore",
    "start": 135.63,
    "end": 136.76
  },
  {
    "text": "that crossed Lake Erie in",
    "start": 136.76,
    "end": 137.86
  },
  {
    "text": "the 1870s passed through brokers",
    "start": 137.86,
    "end": 140.02
  },
  {
    "text": "like him.",
    "start": 140.02,
    "end": 140.44
  },
  {
    "text": "He took a cut.",
    "start": 140.63,
    "end": 141.72
  },
  {
    "text": "Then he bought the newspaper,",
    "start": 141.75,
    "end": 142.88
  },
  {
    "text": "the Cleveland Herald, then a",
    "start": 142.91,
    "end": 144.32
  },
  {
    "text": "theater, then banking interests, then",
    "start": 144.32,
    "end": 146.49
  },
  {
    "text": "a streetcar line.",
    "start": 146.49,
    "end": 147.67
  },
  {
    "text": "By 1880, he controlled enough",
    "start": 147.71,
    "end": 149.24
  },
  {
    "text": "of Cleveland that when he",
    "start": 149.24,
    "end": 150.3
  },
  {
    "text": "walked into a room, the",
    "start": 150.3,
    "end": 151.31
  },
  {
    "text": "room changed temperature and he",
    "start": 151.31,
    "end": 153.24
  },
  {
    "text": "was bored.",
    "start": 153.24,
    "end": 153.79
  },
  {
    "text": "Not with money, he had",
    "start": 153.99,
    "end": 155.15
  },
  {
    "text": "money bored with the ceiling",
    "start": 155.15,
    "end": 156.64
  },
  {
    "text": "because Hanna had figured out.",
    "start": 156.91,
    "end": 158.24
  },
  {
    "text": "Watching the men who supplied",
    "start": 158.27,
    "end": 159.69
  },
  {
    "text": "his coal, the politicians who",
    "start": 159.69,
    "end": 161.22
  },
  {
    "text": "regulated his rail routes, the",
    "start": 161.31,
    "end": 163.03
  },
  {
    "text": "judges who settled his contracts,",
    "start": 163.03,
    "end": 164.88
  },
  {
    "text": "that money was the second",
    "start": 164.91,
    "end": 166.13
  },
  {
    "text": "most powerful thing in America.",
    "start": 166.13,
    "end": 167.88
  },
  {
    "text": "The most powerful thing was",
    "start": 167.91,
    "end": 169.16
  },
  {
    "text": "who decided where the money",
    "start": 169.16,
    "end": 170.56
  },
  {
    "text": "went.",
    "start": 170.56,
    "end": 171.03
  },
  {
    "text": "That was politics and no",
    "start": 171.03,
    "end": 172.48
  },
  {
    "text": "one had ever run it",
    "start": 172.48,
    "end": 173.28
  },
  {
    "text": "like a business, not yet.",
    "start": 173.31,
    "end": 175.04
  },
  {
    "text": "The year was 1888.",
    "start": 175.07,
    "end": 176.88
  },
  {
    "text": "The Republican National Convention, Chicago.",
    "start": 176.99,
    "end": 180.08
  },
  {
    "text": "Mark Hanna arrived not as",
    "start": 180.11,
    "end": 181.44
  },
  {
    "text": "a candidate, but as a",
    "start": 181.44,
    "end": 182.64
  },
  {
    "text": "kingmaker.",
    "start": 182.64,
    "end": 183.36
  },
  {
    "text": "His man was John Sherman.",
    "start": 183.39,
    "end": 184.92
  },
  {
    "text": "Ohio Senator, Treasury veteran, the",
    "start": 185.07,
    "end": 187.5
  },
  {
    "text": "establishment choice.",
    "start": 187.5,
    "end": 188.85
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna worked the convention floor",
    "start": 188.89,
    "end": 190.32
  },
  {
    "text": "for six days trading delegates,",
    "start": 190.32,
    "end": 192.51
  },
  {
    "text": "promising postmasterships, calling in markers",
    "start": 192.51,
    "end": 195.21
  },
  {
    "text": "from Ohio to Pennsylvania.",
    "start": 195.21,
    "end": 196.81
  },
  {
    "text": "Sherman peaked on the first",
    "start": 197.01,
    "end": 198.82
  },
  {
    "text": "ballot at 229 votes.",
    "start": 198.91,
    "end": 200.64
  },
  {
    "text": "Then he bled out, ballot",
    "start": 200.67,
    "end": 202.2
  },
  {
    "text": "after ballot, until the nomination",
    "start": 202.35,
    "end": 204
  },
  {
    "text": "went to Benjamin Harrison on",
    "start": 204.09,
    "end": 205.48
  },
  {
    "text": "the eighth.",
    "start": 205.58,
    "end": 206.36
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna lost, but he saw",
    "start": 206.39,
    "end": 207.86
  },
  {
    "text": "something that weak he would",
    "start": 207.86,
    "end": 209.16
  },
  {
    "text": "never forget.",
    "start": 209.16,
    "end": 209.9
  },
  {
    "text": "A 45-year-old congressman from Canton,",
    "start": 209.99,
    "end": 212.64
  },
  {
    "text": "Ohio had been chairing the",
    "start": 213.08,
    "end": 214.29
  },
  {
    "text": "resolutions committee.",
    "start": 214.29,
    "end": 215.56
  },
  {
    "text": "When delegates began breaking toward",
    "start": 215.59,
    "end": 217.12
  },
  {
    "text": "him as a dark horse",
    "start": 217.27,
    "end": 218.24
  },
  {
    "text": "alternative, the congressman walked to",
    "start": 218.24,
    "end": 220.51
  },
  {
    "text": "the microphone and refused.",
    "start": 220.51,
    "end": 222.16
  },
  {
    "text": "He told the convention he",
    "start": 222.19,
    "end": 223.52
  },
  {
    "text": "was bound to Sherman and",
    "start": 223.52,
    "end": 224.88
  },
  {
    "text": "he sat down.",
    "start": 224.88,
    "end": 225.88
  },
  {
    "text": "That kind of loyalty was",
    "start": 225.91,
    "end": 227.33
  },
  {
    "text": "rare in 1888 politics.",
    "start": 227.33,
    "end": 229.52
  },
  {
    "text": "It was almost extinct.",
    "start": 229.55,
    "end": 231.08
  },
  {
    "text": "His name was William McKinley.",
    "start": 231.11,
    "end": 233.18
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna walked across the floor",
    "start": 233.21,
    "end": 234.74
  },
  {
    "text": "and introduced himself.",
    "start": 234.89,
    "end": 235.87
  },
  {
    "text": "He didn't know it yet,",
    "start": 236.03,
    "end": 237.52
  },
  {
    "text": "but he had just found",
    "start": 237.52,
    "end": 238.46
  },
  {
    "text": "his president.",
    "start": 238.56,
    "end": 239.5
  }
]
